		<!-- SECTION F: ONLINE REVIEWS -->
		<h2>F. Explanation of Missing Online Reviews Due to Closed B2B Business Model</h2>
		<table>
			<tr><th>Subject</th><td>No public sales – no online business, no private customers – internal corporate distribution within the corporate group</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Business Operations</th><td>We act strictly as an internal logistics and distribution intermediary for established commercial partners within a closed network.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>No Public Sales</th><td>No e-commerce, no retail locations, no private customers, and no public-facing marketing or lead generation.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Website Function</th><td>The website exists solely to fulfill regulatory compliance and legal transparency requirements (Imprint, Privacy Policy). No products are advertised or sold online.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Conclusion on Reviews</th><td>Because there is no interaction with the general public or retail consumers, there is no transactional basis for public online ratings (e.g., Google, Trustpilot). The absence of reviews is a direct result of this strictly internal B2B structure and aligns with standard industry practice.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Business Development</th><td>As usual in our industry, new business relationships are only established internally through word-of-mouth and recommendations within the corporate group.</td></tr>
		</table>

		<!-- SECTION G: LEGAL NOTICE -->
		<h2>G. Legal notice regarding imprint obligation &amp; VAT ID</h2>
		<table>
			<tr><th>Subject</th><td>No German imprint obligation for non-European companies – no German VAT ID</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Legal Basis</th><td>An Asian company is not legally obliged to have a registered office in Germany. (Frank Weiß - frank.weiss@ratgeberrecht.eu | <a href="https://www.ratgeberrecht.eu/aktuell/keine-impressumspflicht-fuer-auslaendische-anbieter/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">https://www.ratgeberrecht.eu/aktuell/keine-impressumspflicht-fuer-auslaendische-anbieter/</a>). Because the German imprint obligation according to the so-called country of origin principle generally does not apply to companies with registered office outside the EU. Since ctg-group.eu is registered under Thai law, the Thai business address in the imprint is sufficient.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>VAT ID Clarification</th><td>Information regarding a German sales tax identification number was incorrect. A company solely based in Thailand cannot have a German VAT ID, as this is only issued to companies registered in Germany.</td></tr>
			<tr><th>Signature</th><td>— Chumpol Trading Group Limited Company, Management</td></tr>
		</table>

