		<!-- NEW SECTION I: QUALITY ASSURANCE AND ACCESSIBILITY COMPLIANCE PROTOCOL -->
		<div class="qa-box">
			<h3>I. Quality Assurance & Accessibility Compliance Protocol (Step‑by‑Step Control Loop)</h3>
			<p>To ensure the highest level of completeness, accuracy, and accessibility – especially for users with visual impairments – the following strict quality control steps are applied to every digital output and code document:</p>
			<ol class="qa-step-list">
				<li><strong>Completeness:</strong> The document is written out in full, without any placeholders, comments like "// rest of code here", or omissions. Every word, JSON attribute, and HTML tag is explicitly spelled out.</li>
				<li><strong>Section‑by‑Section Verification:</strong> After each logical section (CSS class, JSON block, HTML section), a verification takes place: All details and sub‑points from the source are exactly implemented. If anything is missing or abbreviated, it is corrected immediately before proceeding.</li>
				<li><strong>Syntax & Structure Check:</strong> After each section, the code is validated: Are all HTML tags correctly opened and closed? Are all table structures (<code>tr</code>, <code>td</code>, <code>th</code>) symmetric and complete? Is all JSON syntactically correct (commas, brackets, quotation marks)?</li>
				<li><strong>Output Guarantee:</strong> The code is never truncated mid‑text. Should the output limit be reached, the code pauses cleanly at the end of a section – but never omits any part of the generated block.</li>
			</ol>
			<p>This protocol serves as a binding internal guideline to prevent hallucinations, speculation, and incomplete code generation, thereby safeguarding both legal compliance and user experience.</p>
		</div>

